\"claim\": \"Evaluator qualification outcome is 'qualified' with status 'completed'; all replications completed (fraction 1.0).\",\n100\t      \"source_ids\": [\n101\t        \"final.qualification.outcome\",\n102\t        \"final.qualification.status\",\n103\t        \"final.qualification.correct\",\n104\t        \"final.metric.completed_replication_fraction\"\n105\t      ]\n106\t    },\n107\t    {\n108\t      \"claim\": \"Null-control absolute bias 0.0173 and constant-world error 0; null-control coverage averaged over N1 and N2 is 0.929 (N1 0.971, N2 0.887).\",\n109\t      \"source_ids\": [\n110\t        \"final.metric.null_control_abs_bias\",\n111\t        \"final.metric.constant_control_error\",\n112\t        \"final.metric.null_control_coverage\",\n113\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n114\t      ]\n115\t    },\n116\t    {\n117\t      \"claim\": \"Seed-level spread over eight seeds: EB-IRT interval score sd 0.0040, naive 0.0234, Bonferroni 0.0036, resampling 0.0251; EB-IRT lower than each baseline in all eight seeds with paired differences 0.075, 0.053, 0.101.\",\n118\t      \"source_ids\": [\n119\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n120\t      ]\n121\t    },\n122\t    {\n123\t      \"claim\": \"Replay-derived (not evaluator-recorded) baseline diagnostics: naive Wilson coverage 0.713 (sd 0.048) and width 0.109; Bonferroni-Wilson coverage 0.962, width 0.190; resampling coverage 0.748, width 0.104 (aggregate over P1-P6). The evaluator records only baseline interval scores and the naive bias; the replay reproduced those recorded values exactly (max abs difference 0), and the other replayed quantities are unchecked against any record.\",\n124\t      \"source_ids\": [\n125\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n126\t        \"final.metric.naive_baseline_score\"\n127\t      ]\n128\t    },\n129\t    {\n130\t      \"claim\": \"Naive bias on real exhaustive cases falls with N: 0.051 (N=60), 0.022 (N=200), 0.009 (N=600).\",\n131\t      \"source_ids\": [\n132\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n133\t      ]\n134\t    },\n135\t    {\n136\t      \"claim\": \"Final-pool configuration accuracies range from 0.107 to 0.166 (task manifest); naive optimism at N=60 (0.051) is of the same order as the spread of configuration pool accuracies (0.107 to 0.166); no inference about reported advantage over alternatives.\",\n137\t      \"source_ids\": [\n138\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n139\t      ]\n140\t    },\n141\t    {\n142\t      \"claim\": \"Naive bias in null worlds: 0.067 in N1 vs 0.049 in P1; 0.034 in N2 vs 0.022 in P3.\",\n143\t      \"source_ids\": [\n144\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n145\t      ]\n146\t    },\n147\t    {\n148\t      \"claim\": \"Searcher effect on naive bias: P2 0.054, P4 0.025 vs P1 0.049, P3 0.022; matched paired differences +0.004 (sd 0.012) and +0.003 (sd 0.008); aggregated naive bias 0.036 for both searchers.\",\n149\t      \"source_ids\": [\n150\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n151\t      ]\n152\t    },\n153\t    {\n154\t      \"claim\": \"Per-case EB-IRT vs naive interval scores: P1 0.150 vs 0.264, P2 0.155 vs 0.300, P5 0.192 vs 0.303; reductions of 37-48%; coverage 0.96, 0.96, 0.98.\",\n155\t      \"source_ids\": [\n156\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n157\t      ]\n158\t    },\n159\t    {\n160\t      \"claim\": \"P4: EB-IRT 0.156 vs naive 0.161 and Bonferroni 0.165; wins in six of eight seeds; bias 0.031 vs 0.025; coverage 0.89 (slightly below nominal, within about one standard error over eight seeds; seed sd about 0.03). P6: all Wilson-style reporters 0.096; coverage 0.83 (seed sd 0.05), clearly below nominal.\",\n161\t      \"source_ids\": [\n162\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n163\t      ]\n164\t    },\n165\t    {\n166\t      \"claim\": \"Exhaustive-search restricted aggregate: EB-IRT 0.1406, resampling 0.1405, naive 0.2166; halving cases: resampling 0.3916 vs EB-IRT 0.1556.\",\n167\t      \"source_ids\": [\n168\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n169\t      ]\n170\t    },\n171\t    {\n172\t      \"claim\": \"Resampling is slightly better than EB-IRT in P3 (0.109 vs 0.116), P5 (0.174 vs 0.192) and N2 (0.102 vs 0.111); EB-IRT better in 2, 1 and 1 of 8 seeds.\",\n173\t      \"source_ids\": [\n174\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n175\t      ]\n176\t    },\n177\t    {\n178\t      \"claim\": \"Replay-derived (resampling bias and coverage are not evaluator-recorded; replay reproduced the recorded baseline interval scores and naive bias exactly): resampling over-corrects under halving with bias -0.067 (P2) and -0.031 (P4), and coverage 0.44 and 0.61; aggregate resampling bias -0.0209.\",\n179\t      \"source_ids\": [\n180\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n181\t      ]\n182\t    },\n183\t    {\n184\t      \"claim\": \"EB-IRT signed bias positive in five of six primary cases (0.009-0.031) and -0.002 (sd 0.010) in P1.\",\n185\t      \"source_ids\": [\n186\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n187\t      ]\n188\t    },\n189\t    {\n190\t      \"claim\": \"Interval widths at N=60/200/600: EB-IRT 0.187/0.101/0.065, naive 0.167/0.088/0.050, Bonferroni-Wilson 0.284/0.153/0.088.\",\n191\t      \"source_ids\": [\n192\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n193\t      ]\n194\t    },\n195\t    {\n196\t      \"claim\": \"Controls: N1 EB-IRT coverage 0.971, interval score 0.128 vs naive 0.354 (naive coverage 0.47); N2 EB-IRT coverage 0.887, score 0.111 vs naive 0.218 and resampling 0.102; Z1 interval [0,0.02], score 0.020 vs naive 0.026 and Bonferroni 0.059.\",\n197\t      \"source_ids\": [\n198\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n199\t        \"final.metric.constant_control_error\"\n200\t      ]\n201\t    },\n202\t    {\n203\t      \"claim\": \"Width factor kappa ranges from 1.43 to 1.63 across the evaluated cases (computed from the reporter's own function).\",\n204\t      \"source_ids\": [\n205\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n206\t      ]\n207\t    },\n208\t    {\n209\t      \"claim\": \"Development-setting variants (4 seeds): EB-IRT interval score 0.1480, coverage 0.915, width 0.124; config-by-subject variant 0.1519, coverage 0.893; bootstrap pivot variant 0.1562, coverage 0.77, width 0.085; baselines 0.2321 (naive), 0.1961 (Bonferroni), 0.2732 (resampling).\",\n210\t      \"source_ids\": [\n211\t        \"result.top_program_01\",\n212\t        \"result.top_program_02\",\n213\t        \"result.top_program_03\",\n214\t        \"result.total_evaluated_programs\"\n215\t      ]\n216\t    },\n217\t    {\n218\t      \"claim\": \"Three reporter variants were evaluated once each in the development setting; all three were scored.\",\n219\t      \"source_ids\": [\n220\t        \"result.total_attempts\",\n221\t        \"result.total_evaluated_programs\",\n222\t        \"result.total_correct_programs\"\n223\t      ]\n224\t    },\n225\t    {\n226\t      \"claim\": \"Evaluator-recorded wall-clock time averaged 6.2 s per seed (250 episodes, reporter calls plus scoring), about 50 s over the eight sealed seeds; 2000 episodes in total.\",\n227\t      \"source_ids\": [\n228\t        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n229\t      ]\n230\t    },\n231\t    {\n232\t      \"citation_keys\": [\n233\t        \"Gneiting2007Scoring\"\n234\t      ],\n235\t      \"claim\": \"Interval score is a proper scoring rule minimized by the 5% and 95% predictive quantiles.\",\n236\t      \"source_ids\": [\n237\t        \"final.metric.mean_interval_score\"\n238\t      ]\n239\t    },\n240\t    {\n241\t      \"citation_keys\": [\n242\t        \"Dwork2014PreservingSV\",\n243\t        \"Dwork2015GeneralizationIA\",\n244\t        \"Dwork2015TheRH\",\n245\t        \"Feldman2017CalibratingNT\",\n246\t        \"Hardt2014Hard\",\n247\t        \"Blum2015Ladder\",\n248\t        \"Berk2013ValidPSI\",\n249\t        \"Andrews2024InferenceOnWinners\",\n250\t        \"Chernozhukov2013Gaussian\",\n251\t        \"Efron1973Stein\",\n252\t        \"Efron2011Tweedie\",\n253\t        \"Efron1997Bootstrap632\",\n254\t        \"Recht2019ImageNet\",\n255\t       